  <section class="section" id="general" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">General</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">General questions about the platform.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What is Teamwork Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is a global, AI-enabled retail platform that natively integrates enterprise POS, OMS, Inventory Management, RFID, and AI into one system. It powers 30,000+ terminals across 40+ countries with open APIs, serving mid-market and enterprise retailers in fashion, footwear, stadiums, museums, jewelry, and specialty retail.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce handle offline transactions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The POS keeps selling through a network outage, because the app and its data are on the device rather than in a browser tab. Card data is encrypted at the point of capture, on the payment terminal or Tap to Pay on iPhone, and never stored on the POS. Sales queue locally and sync to the back office automatically when connectivity returns. Offline card acceptance depends on the payment provider you use.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What makes the RFID solution different from competitors?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce offers an industry-leading native RFID stack, no third-party middleware required. It covers tag encoding at receiving, RFID-enabled checkout (scan an entire basket in one tap), real-time item-level tracking, and full-store cycle counts in minutes. This delivers 99.9% inventory accuracy.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What is the AI at the point of sale?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>It is an AI assistant built into the associate's handheld device, there to help associates help their customers. Instead of digging through binders or radioing the back room, an associate asks a question the way they would ask a colleague and gets an answer, with pictures, in seconds. They can describe what the customer wants in plain language (“something warm for a weekend in the mountains”), scan a tag to pull up product information, or browse by category to see what is new, then save and share products. Faster answers mean less time searching and more time selling, and customers leave with exactly what they came for, or something even better.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Is Teamwork Commerce SOC 2 compliant?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce holds SOC 2 Type 2, and is GDPR and PCI DSS compliant. SOC 2 coverage for a given deployment is confirmed as part of your agreement. The platform also supports fiscal compliance standards including NF525 (France) and TSE (Germany) across 40+ countries.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How long does deployment take?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Implementations typically run from around 120 days to two years, depending on fleet size, operational complexity, and how many integrations are in scope. Our own service team leads every implementation, working alongside any systems integrator or technology partner you bring. Once a retailer is live, opening an additional store is a matter of hours rather than a project.</p></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="mobile-pos" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">Mobile POS</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">From the <a href="/platform/mobile-pos/" style="color: var(--brand-text); font-weight: 600;">Mobile POS</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Why is Teamwork Commerce the preferred POS for global enterprise retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is a natively global, end-to-end DTC retail platform that unifies POS, inventory management, RFID, shipping/receiving, pricing, promotions, and loyalty within a single codebase. That means fewer vendors to manage, with fiscal compliance handled in 40+ countries. Unlike competitors that require third-party middleware for RFID or separate regional vendors for compliance, Teamwork delivers everything in one integrated iOS-native system.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce handle offline transactions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The POS keeps selling through a network outage, because the app and its data are on the device rather than in a browser tab. Card data is encrypted at the point of capture, on the payment terminal or Tap to Pay on iPhone, and never stored on the POS. Sales queue locally and sync to the back office automatically when connectivity returns. Offline card acceptance depends on the payment provider you use. This matters for stadiums, pop-up events, and regions with unreliable connectivity.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Is the platform SOC 2 compliant?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce holds SOC 2 Type 2, and is GDPR and PCI DSS compliant. SOC 2 coverage for a given deployment is confirmed as part of your agreement. Enterprise-grade security protects PII and financial data across all global touchpoints.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How long does it take to train associates on the POS?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The interface follows iOS patterns associates already know, so time to a first transaction is short: seasonal staff at the Colorado Rockies were on registers in as little as 5 minutes. That is time to a first sale rather than the whole training program, which runs as instructor-led sessions plus role-based courses in the platform as part of every implementation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Does the POS support RFID checkout?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce offers an industry-leading native RFID stack, no third-party middleware. RFID-enabled checkout processes entire baskets in seconds without line-of-sight scanning. Next-gen self-checkout kiosks auto-detect items. The system delivers 99.9% inventory accuracy at item level.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to other unified commerce POS platforms?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The practical difference is where RFID lives. Most platforms in this category reach it through a third-party integration layer, so tag reads arrive as an import after the fact. Ours runs inside the POS, which is why receiving, counting, transferring and selling all operate by individual EPC. The iOS-native architecture, the AI agent and the 30+ years behind the product matter too, but RFID is the one that changes how a store actually works.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to an e-commerce-first POS for enterprise retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Shopify POS is built for high-volume DTC and SMB retail, with point of sale as an extension of its e-commerce platform. Teamwork Commerce is built the other way, POS first, for the physical store, with native RFID, offline resilience on the device, and AI built in. For enterprise retailers running fiscal compliance across 40+ countries and RFID-driven inventory accuracy, Teamwork Commerce is purpose-built for that scale; Shopify POS is purpose-built for fast-growing DTC brands.</p></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
