  <section class="section" id="order-management" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">Order Management</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">From the <a href="/platform/oms/" style="color: var(--brand-text); font-weight: 600;">Order Management</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What makes Teamwork Commerce OMS different from standalone order management systems?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork's OMS is natively integrated with POS and Inventory rather than bolted on through middleware, so order-fill decisions read the same live stock record the store is selling from. You configure the fill logic yourself, ranking strategies by stock depth and node capacity and setting rules by store, region, channel or SKU, and safety stock per location holds a popular line back for the shop floor. Where a retailer runs RFID, the counts behind that record are verified to 99.9% accuracy.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Order Fill Logic decide where to fulfill an order?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Order Fill Logic is a ranked, configurable rule stack. You set the priority, for example fill complete from the highest-stock location, ship-to-store for pickup orders, or ship-from-vendor, and the engine applies your rules to every order against live stock. It can also split an order across nodes when a single location cannot fill it. It does not rate-shop carriers or route by distance, and it does not calculate margin.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can Teamwork Commerce OMS handle ship-from-store and BOPIS?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Ship-from-store turns every retail location into a fulfillment node with pick-and-pack tasks for store associates. BOPIS (Buy Online Pick Up In Store) promises against the live stock record rather than an overnight file, so the item is there when the customer arrives. Buy Online Return In Store (BORIS) is also natively supported.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this order management compare to other unified commerce platforms?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>New Black EVA offers scoring-based order orchestration but requires third-party middleware for RFID. NewStore focuses heavily on fulfillment but doesn't offer native RFID or merchandising intelligence. What Teamwork Commerce does differently is run order routing on inventory it can actually trust: Order Fill Logic is configurable, and the RFID underneath it is native rather than middleware, so stock is accurate to 99.9% before a routing decision is made.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Does the OMS support multi-currency and multi-entity operations?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The OMS operates across multiple legal entities and currencies, and a US-based HQ can manage global operations while regional teams work in their local currency and language. Fiscal compliance itself sits with the POS and with the ERP: the OMS hands the order, tender and stock movement across so the books are closed in the system that owns them.</p></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

