  <section class="section" id="inventory-control" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">Inventory Control</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">From the <a href="/platform/inventory-control/" style="color: var(--brand-text); font-weight: 600;">Inventory Control</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce achieve 99.9% inventory accuracy?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Through an industry-leading native RFID stack. RFID-powered cycle counts scan thousands of items in minutes without pulling product off racks. Real-time reconciliation updates global stock levels instantly. Combined with AI anomaly detection that flags suspicious inventory movement, this is what holds inventory at 99.9% accuracy and keeps ghost SKUs out of the count.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can cycle counts be done without closing the store?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Rolling RFID cycle counts run during business hours, with associates scanning on the mobile POS while customers shop. Stock keeps moving while you count, so a count taken during trading will surface discrepancies that have to be reconciled. That is a logistics problem rather than a software one, and no system removes it. A typical 10-store chain recovers $150,000–$300,000 in previously "lost" stock within the first 12 months of switching to weekly RFID counts.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does the AI predict stock-outs before they happen?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The AI monitors the velocity of RFID tags moving through the sales floor. When it detects a SKU approaching zero at a location, it automatically queues a transfer from the nearest warehouse or store with surplus stock. It can also trigger vendor re-orders.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this inventory compare to other unified commerce platforms?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce has native RFID from receiving through checkout, with no third-party middleware. This means cycle counts, receiving, loss prevention and real-time tracking share the same records, with no integration points to break. The result: 99.9% inventory accuracy.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Does the system work offline?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Inventory operations keep running through a network outage. Receiving, counts, adjustments, and transfers continue on the device, then sync automatically when connectivity returns.</p></div>
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="ai-assistant" style="padding-top: 40px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h2 class="section-title" style="font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px);">AI</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" style="margin: 4px 0 0;">From the <a href="/features/customer-data/" style="color: var(--brand-text); font-weight: 600;">customer data</a> page.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="max-width: 800px;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What is the AI at the point of sale?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>It is an AI assistant built into the associate's handheld device, there to help associates help their customers. Instead of digging through binders or radioing the back room, an associate asks a question the way they would ask a colleague and gets an answer, with pictures, in seconds. They can describe what the customer wants in plain language (“something warm for a weekend in the mountains”), scan a tag to pull up product information, or browse by category to see what is new, then save and share products. Faster answers mean less time searching and more time selling, and customers leave with exactly what they came for, or something even better.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How do product data and customer data work together?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The product record is the foundation, it unifies all product knowledge including descriptions, materials, care instructions, imagery, and translations. Customer data builds on the product record by capturing every customer interaction as a selling ceremony, storing associate feedback, and using that data to continuously refine the AI Agent's recommendations. Together they create a self-improving intelligence loop.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does the AI learn and improve over time?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every customer interaction is captured as a customer session. After each session, associates can provide feedback and corrections, strengthening the AI's understanding of your customers and products. This feedback loop means the AI gets more accurate with every interaction. The sooner your product and customer data are centralized, the faster the AI accumulates the knowledge it needs.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can the selling session continue after the customer leaves the store?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. When a customer leaves the store, the AI Agent carries the interaction forward. If the customer browses your website at home that evening, the AI can surface recommendations based on what they tried in-store, what the associate noted, and what's been wishlisted, so the experience stays personal across channels.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does the AI relate to the Teamwork Commerce platform?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Product data and customer data are shared services within the Teamwork Commerce platform, the same product and customer intelligence layers that power other apps across the platform. The AI is where they converge at the point of sale: real-time associate guidance, backed by the same product data and customer intelligence the platform runs on. The secure identity layer sits underneath the same experience.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How is the AI different from other retail AI solutions?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Most retail AI focuses on e-commerce recommendations or customer-facing chatbots. Ours is built for the associate, it's a co-pilot for the physical sales floor. It's natively integrated with Teamwork's POS, OMS, RFID, and inventory systems, so recommendations are backed by real-time stock data, customer history, and product intelligence. No other platform offers this depth of AI natively integrated with the full retail stack.</p></div>
