        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is not a repair or appraisal system, and it does not handle trade-ins. It integrates tightly with the systems that do. The associate takes the deposit in Teamwork Commerce, the repair goes to your repair system, and its status comes back so the customer can be told the piece is ready to collect.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can Teamwork modernize our black books while staying GDPR compliant?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The unified CRM stores sizes, style preferences, purchase history, wishlists and associate notes, so the same client record follows a shopper between stores and channels, fully GDPR compliant with data protection built into the architecture. The AI uses this data to surface recommendations in real time. The client profile follows the customer whether they visit Paris, London, or Milan.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Does the POS fit the luxury in-store aesthetic?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is 100% native iOS. The interface is sleek, minimal, and designed for the luxury environment, no industrial hardware, no clunky terminals. Associates complete transactions on iPad or iPhone anywhere in the boutique, creating a personal shopping experience without interrupting the brand atmosphere.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to other POS platforms for luxury retail?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is built for luxury's scarcity and clienteling requirements. Luxury puts weight on two things most platforms treat as secondary: knowing exactly what exists when a run is small, and knowing the client well enough to call them about it. RFID precision covers the first; clienteling and deposit handling cover the second. The iOS interface and compliance in 40+ countries are table stakes at this level.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
