          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The Colorado Rockies put new associates on registers in five minutes after they start. The iOS interface follows familiar design patterns that most people already know. For stadium retail where staff might work 20 games a year, that keeps training down.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does this compare to stadium-merchandise-only POS systems?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is a broader platform than a stadium-merchandise-only system: native RFID (not third-party), offline resilience (critical for network-saturated venues), integrated OMS with Endless Aisle and ship-from-store, real-time AI fan loyalty through the LAVA and Givex partnerships, and the full omnichannel stack (BOPIS, BORIS, cross-channel inventory). For venues that also operate standalone retail stores, like InnovaSport's 250 locations, the same deployment extends from the stadium to the entire retail fleet.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          What fan spending data is available?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>The cloud back office provides sales analytics by game period (pre-game, halftime, post-game), per-fan average spend, terminal performance, product velocity, and inventory turnover. In a Mashgin survey of MLB fans, 53% wait 15 minutes or more at concession stands and over 80% have abandoned a purchase because the line was too long, and venues offering mobile ordering see per-capita spend rise 22%.</p></div>
